        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ತಲೆಬಾಗು",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ತಲೆಬಾಗು — talebāgu — \"to bow down; to give in\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಒತ್ತಡಕ್ಕೆ ತಲೆಬಾಗಿ ಕಂಪನಿ ಸಂಬಳ ಹೆಚ್ಚಿಸಿತು. ottaḍakke talebāgi kampani sambaḷa heccisitu. Giving in to pressure, the company raised pay."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (I …): ತಲೆಬಾಗಿದೆ, talebāgide."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ತಲೆ (head) + ಬಾಗು (to bend). What one gives in to takes -ಗೆ."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ತಲೆಬಾಗು (talebāgu) is native Dravidian, built from tale, \"head\" (DEDR 3103), and bāgu, \"to bend, to bow\" (DEDR 5335)."
            }
          ]
        },
